window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2c7688c996bc9669"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"get-started-with-chatgpt-work\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-work\">开始使用 ChatGPT Work</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">媒体内容 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/superapp-video-v1.mp4\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/superapp-video-v1.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"introducing-work-mode\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"introducing-chatgpt-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work_1\">认识 ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>ChatGPT Work 可以把实际工作委派给 ChatGPT 完成。</p> <p>如果你只需要一个答案、解释、头脑风暴或简短草稿，请使用 Chat。如果你希望 ChatGPT 完成有明确结果的任务，例如制作简报、演示文稿、分析、定期更新、工作流或可供你审阅和使用的文件，请使用 ChatGPT Work。了解如何<a href=\"#/article/a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f\">搭配使用 Chat 和 ChatGPT Work</a>。</p> <p>ChatGPT Work 可以使用你的文件、插件和经批准的工具来查找信息、创建完整文件、运行工作流，并完成可供你审阅的工作。你可以跟踪进度、回答问题、调整方向，并批准重要操作。</p> <p>在<a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">桌面应用</a>中，如果相应工具可用，ChatGPT Work 还可以使用本地文件、应用和浏览器。</p> <p>如果你曾使用 Codex 处理非编程工作，可以继续使用 Codex，也可以改用 ChatGPT Work。ChatGPT Work 具备相同的核心能力，但提供了更适合日常工作的体验。</p> <p>有关一般用法和可用性的信息，请参阅帮助中心中的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001275\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Work 和 Codex（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-try-first\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">首先试试这些</h2> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">媒体内容 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/videos-learn/selectnoonboarding.mp4\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/videos-learn/selectnoonboarding.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>先切换到 <strong>Work</strong>，然后选择第一个任务。好的任务有明确的结果、少量源材料，以及可供你检查的输出。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-work-across-devices\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"work\">在不同设备间继续 Work</h3> <p>当工作区启用同步后，使用 Work Cloud 和本地计算机访问功能的任务会通过云端协调。对于 Enterprise（企业版）用户，应用内的 Local/Cloud（本地/云端）切换开关及其默认设置在功能上线时保持不变。你可以在桌面、手机和网页上继续符合条件的对话。Work 仍可通过已连接的计算机使用经批准的本地资源。</p> <p>例如，你可以在笔记本电脑上使用一个已获批准的文件夹开始任务，然后在手机上检查结果或发送后续指示。如果后续步骤需要访问电脑上的文件或工具，请让笔记本电脑保持联网。</p> <p>启用同步后，请新建一个任务。已有任务（包括项目中的任务）仍仅在本地运行，或留在云端但无法访问本地文件。</p> <p>如果新一轮对话开始时你的电脑不可用，符合条件且使用 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问功能的已有任务可以继续在云容器中运行。但该容器无法访问那台电脑上的文件或工具，也无法执行企业对本地执行的要求。Work 不能在一轮执行过程中从本地切换到云端。</p> <p>如果没有启用 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问功能，请在桌面端输入框中选择本地或云端选项。需要使用电脑资源时选择本地 Work；不依赖电脑资源的任务则选择云端 Work。对于需要研究或检查网站的定时任务，使用云端很方便，因为你的电脑不必一直开机。</p> <p>关闭 Work Cloud 本地计算机访问功能会中断正在运行的轮次。要继续在 Work Cloud 中处理已有云端对话且不访问本地文件，请发送一条新消息。</p> <p>工作区管理员可以先查看<a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=how-to-set-up-local-computer-access\">策略要求和设置步骤</a>，再启用同步。</p> <p>下面介绍三种常见用法：</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-presentation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">创建演示文稿</h3> <p>使用 ChatGPT Work 将笔记、文档、研究资料或会议材料整理成结构清晰的演示文稿。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：使用 ChatGPT Work 创建的演示文稿。</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>示例提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the attached source materials and create an eight-slide presentation for [audience]. Focus on the main themes, include supporting evidence, and flag anything that needs human review. Return a draft for my review.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文提示词：请查看附件中的资料，并为[受众]制作一份八页演示文稿。聚焦主要主题，提供支持性证据，并标出需要人工审阅的内容。先返回草稿供我审阅。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"create-a-comparison-spreadsheet\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">创建对比用电子表格</h3> <p>使用 ChatGPT Work 将笔记、文件或研究资料整理成比较不同选项并帮助你作出决定的电子表格。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：使用 ChatGPT Work 创建的对比电子表格。</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>示例提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a spreadsheet comparing the options for [decision]. Use the attached notes and source materials. Include the most important criteria, score each option, flag risks or missing information, and add a summary tab with a recommendation and next steps.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文提示词：请制作一份电子表格，比较适合[决策事项]的各个选项。使用附件中的笔记和资料，列出最重要的标准，为每个选项评分，标出风险或缺失信息，并添加一个摘要工作表，给出建议和后续步骤。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"set-up-a-recurring-update\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">设置定期更新</h3> <p>如果你希望 ChatGPT Work 持续重复、监控或刷新某项内容，请使用定时任务。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：使用 ChatGPT Work 设置的定期更新任务。</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>示例提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Every Monday morning, review new updates from @Slack and @Google Drive for [project]. Refresh the meeting agenda with decisions, blockers, owners, and open questions. Send me a draft before sharing it.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文提示词：每周一早上，查看 @Slack 和 @Google Drive 中有关[项目]的最新动态。更新会议议程，列出决策、阻碍事项、负责人和未解决问题。在分享之前先把草稿发给我。</p> </blockquote> <p>了解更多<a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">定时任务</a>相关信息。</p> <p><a id=\"best-practices-for-using-work\"></a> <a id=\"best-practices-for-using-work-mode\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"best-practices-for-using-chatgpt-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work_2\">使用 ChatGPT Work 的最佳实践</h2> <p>如果你希望 ChatGPT 完成任务、创建文件或长期管理某项工作，请使用 ChatGPT Work。它适用于以下任务：</p> <ul> <li>需要使用多个来源、插件、工具或步骤。</li> <li>手动完成需要花费相当多时间。</li> <li>会产出你可以审阅、编辑或重复使用的结果。</li> <li>需要定期重复、监控或更新。</li> </ul> <p>为了获得更好的结果，请告诉 ChatGPT 你需要的结果、要使用的来源或插件、必须遵守的约束、怎样才算做好，以及何时应停下来等待审阅或批准。</p> <p><strong>不要只说：</strong>“给我做一份关于客户研究的演示文稿。”</p> <p><strong>示例提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the attached interview notes and survey results. Create an eight-slide presentation for the product leadership meeting. Focus on the three most common customer problems, include supporting evidence, separate findings from recommendations, and flag any claims that are not well supported. Use @Google Drive for the source docs. Return a draft for my review before treating it as final.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文提示词：请审阅附件中的访谈笔记和调查结果，为产品管理层会议制作一份八页演示文稿。聚焦最常见的三个客户问题，提供支持性证据，将发现与建议分开，并标出依据不足的说法。使用 @Google Drive 中的源文档。先返回草稿供我审阅，在我确认前不要视为最终版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>了解更多关于<a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=prompting-for-work\">如何为 ChatGPT Work 编写提示词</a>的信息。</p> <p><a id=\"add-plugins-for-more-context-and-better-outputs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">添加插件以获得更多上下文和更好的输出</h2> <blockquote> <p>插图：ChatGPT Work 中的插件库。</p> </blockquote> <p>插件可以将 ChatGPT Work 连接到团队使用的工具，例如 Slack、Google Drive、SharePoint、电子邮件、日历、客户关系管理系统和项目跟踪工具。</p> <ul> <li>在左侧导航中选择 <strong>Customize（自定义）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>，查看插件库。</li> <li>安装最适合你工作的插件。</li> <li>如果要指定某个工具，请在提示词中输入 <code>@</code> 和插件名称。</li> </ul> <p>了解更多关于<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>的信息。要让工作流可以重复使用，可以通过与 ChatGPT 对话来<a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">创建和编辑插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"use-work-mode-efficiently\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-chatgpt-work-efficiently\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work_3\">高效使用 ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>对于需要仔细推理、视觉判断或精致成品文件的高难度工作，请选择 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</a>。如果希望以低于 Astra 的成本处理复杂工作，可以考虑 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a>；较简单的任务则可以考虑 Luna。请从模型选择器中选择当前可用的模型，并在开始大型任务前查看<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">套餐用量</a>。</p> <p>ChatGPT Work 最适合涉及多个步骤、来源或工具，或需要交付完整成果的重要任务。任务越长或越复杂，ChatGPT 代表你完成的工作越多，因此可能会消耗更多额度。评估时应关注完成结果的价值，而不是提示词的数量。</p> <p>请通过设置有用的边界让任务保持聚焦。例如：“只使用这些来源”“比较排名前五的选项”或“在发送任何内容之前停止”。</p> <p>快速提问、简短改写，以及只需要建议的决策，请改用 Chat。</p> <p>了解更多关于<a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=prompting-for-work\">高效工作的方式</a>。</p> <p>如果任务因安全审查而暂停，请按照提示操作，并在继续之前查看可用的发现结果。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=safety-monitoring-and-paused-tasks\">安全监控和已暂停的任务</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"more-use-cases\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">更多使用场景</h2> <p>探索适用于常见团队和任务的 ChatGPT Work 实用工作流。</p> <p><strong>相关集合</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>productivity-and-collaboration</code></li> <li><code>business-operations</code></li> <li><code>data-science</code></li> <li><code>finance</code></li> <li><code>sales</code></li> <li><code>life-sciences</code></li> <li><code>education</code></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"get-started-with-chatgpt-work\">Get started with ChatGPT Work</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">媒体内容 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/superapp-video-v1.mp4\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/superapp-video-v1.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"introducing-work-mode\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"introducing-chatgpt-work\">Introducing ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>ChatGPT Work is a way to delegate real work to ChatGPT.</p> <p>Use Chat when you want an answer, explanation, brainstorm, or short draft. Use ChatGPT Work when you want ChatGPT to complete a task with a clear outcome, such as a brief, deck, analysis, recurring update, workflow, or file you can review and use. Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-d6b5aa6a43ce8c0f\">using Chat and ChatGPT Work together</a>.</p> <p>ChatGPT Work can use your files, plugins, and approved tools to retrieve information, create finished files, run workflows, and complete work that is ready for you to review. You can follow progress, answer questions, change direction, and approve important actions.</p> <p>On the <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">desktop app</a>, ChatGPT Work can also use local files, apps, and the browser when those tools are available.</p> <p>If you have used Codex for non-coding work, you can stay in Codex or use ChatGPT Work instead. ChatGPT Work gives you the same core capabilities with an experience designed for everyday work.</p> <p>For general usage and availability, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001275\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT Work and Codex (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-try-first\">What to try first</h2> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">媒体内容 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/videos-learn/selectnoonboarding.mp4\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/videos-learn/selectnoonboarding.mp4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>First, switch to <strong>Work</strong>. Then choose your first task. Good tasks have a clear outcome, a few source materials, and an output you can review.</p> <h3 id=\"continue-work-across-devices\">Continue Work across devices</h3> <p>When your workspace enables sync, tasks using Local computer access with Work Cloud use cloud coordination. For enterprises, the in-app Local/Cloud toggle and its default remain unchanged at launch. You can continue an eligible conversation across desktop, mobile, and web. Work can still use approved local resources through a connected computer.</p> <p>For example, start a task with an approved folder on your laptop, then review results or send follow-up instructions from your phone. Keep the laptop online for steps that need its files or tools.</p> <p>Start a new task after enabling sync. Existing tasks, including those in projects, stay local only or in the cloud without access to local files.</p> <p>If your computer is unavailable when a new turn starts, an existing eligible task using Local computer access with Work Cloud can continue in a cloud container. The container cannot access that computer's files or tools or enforce its enterprise execution requirements. Work can't switch from local to cloud execution during a turn.</p> <p>Without Local computer access with Work Cloud, use the desktop composer's local and cloud options. Choose local Work for resources on your computer, or cloud Work for tasks that don't depend on it. Cloud is useful for scheduled tasks that research or check websites because your computer doesn't need to be awake.</p> <p>Turning off Local computer access with Work Cloud interrupts running turns. Send a new message in an existing cloud conversation to continue in Work Cloud without access to local files.</p> <p>Workspace admins can review <a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=how-to-set-up-local-computer-access\">policy requirements and setup steps</a> before enabling sync.</p> <p>Here are three common use cases you can get started with:</p> <h3 id=\"create-a-presentation\">Create a presentation</h3> <p>Use ChatGPT Work to turn notes, docs, research, or meeting materials into a structured deck.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A presentation created in ChatGPT Work</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Example prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the attached source materials and create an eight-slide presentation for [audience]. Focus on the main themes, include supporting evidence, and flag anything that needs human review. Return a draft for my review.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"create-a-comparison-spreadsheet\">Create a comparison spreadsheet</h3> <p>Use ChatGPT Work to turn notes, files, or research into a spreadsheet that compares options and helps you make a decision.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A comparison spreadsheet created in ChatGPT Work</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Example prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a spreadsheet comparing the options for [decision]. Use the attached notes and source materials. Include the most important criteria, score each option, flag risks or missing information, and add a summary tab with a recommendation and next steps.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"set-up-a-recurring-update\">Set up a recurring update</h3> <p>Use scheduled tasks when you want ChatGPT Work to repeat, monitor, or refresh something over time.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A recurring update scheduled in ChatGPT Work</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Example prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Every Monday morning, review new updates from @Slack and @Google Drive for [project]. Refresh the meeting agenda with decisions, blockers, owners, and open questions. Send me a draft before sharing it.\n</code></pre> <p>Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">scheduled tasks</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"best-practices-for-using-work\"></a> <a id=\"best-practices-for-using-work-mode\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"best-practices-for-using-chatgpt-work\">Best practices for using ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>Use ChatGPT Work when you want ChatGPT to complete a task, create a file, or manage work over time. Use it for tasks that:</p> <ul> <li>Use multiple sources, plugins, tools, or steps.</li> <li>Would take meaningful time to complete manually.</li> <li>Produce an output you will review, edit, or reuse.</li> <li>Need to be repeated, monitored, or updated over time.</li> </ul> <p>To get a better result, tell ChatGPT the outcome you need, the sources or plugins to use, any constraints to follow, what good looks like, and when to stop for review or approval.</p> <p><strong>Instead of:</strong> Make me a presentation about our customer research.</p> <p><strong>Example prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the attached interview notes and survey results. Create an eight-slide presentation for the product leadership meeting. Focus on the three most common customer problems, include supporting evidence, separate findings from recommendations, and flag any claims that are not well supported. Use @Google Drive for the source docs. Return a draft for my review before treating it as final.\n</code></pre> <p>Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=prompting-for-work\">prompting for ChatGPT Work</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"add-plugins-for-more-context-and-better-outputs\">Add plugins for more context and better outputs</h2> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: The plugins library in ChatGPT Work</p> </blockquote> <p>Plugins connect ChatGPT Work to tools your team uses, like Slack, Google Drive, SharePoint, email, calendars, customer relationship management systems, and project trackers.</p> <ul> <li>Select <strong>Customize</strong>, then <strong>Plugins</strong>, in the left navigation to view the plugins library.</li> <li>Install the plugins most relevant to your work.</li> <li>To point ChatGPT to a specific tool, type <code>@</code> and the plugin name in your prompt.</li> </ul> <p>Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">plugins</a>. To make a workflow reusable, <a href=\"#/article/a-0d81218eacd2463c\">create and edit a plugin</a> through a conversation with ChatGPT.</p> <p><a id=\"use-work-mode-efficiently\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"use-chatgpt-work-efficiently\">Use ChatGPT Work efficiently</h2> <p>Choose <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6-astra\">GPT-6 Astra</a> for demanding work that needs careful reasoning, visual judgment, or a polished final file. Consider <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a> for complex work at a lower cost than Astra, or Luna for simpler tasks. Select from the models available in your model selector and check <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">plan usage</a> before starting a large task.</p> <p>ChatGPT Work is best for substantial tasks that involve multiple steps, sources, or tools, or require a completed deliverable. Longer or more complex tasks may use more credits because ChatGPT is doing more on your behalf. Focus on the value of the completed result, rather than the number of prompts.</p> <p>Keep the task focused by setting useful boundaries. For example: “use only these sources,” “compare the top five options,” or “stop before sending anything.”</p> <p>Use Chat instead for quick questions, short rewrites, and decisions where you only need advice.</p> <p>Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=prompting-for-work\">working efficiently</a>.</p> <p>If a task pauses for a safety review, follow the notice and review any available findings before continuing. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=safety-monitoring-and-paused-tasks\">safety monitoring and paused tasks</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"more-use-cases\">More use cases</h2> <p>Explore practical ChatGPT Work workflows for common teams and tasks.</p> <p><strong>Related collections</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>productivity-and-collaboration</code></li> <li><code>business-operations</code></li> <li><code>data-science</code></li> <li><code>finance</code></li> <li><code>sales</code></li> <li><code>life-sciences</code></li> <li><code>education</code></li> </ul>"};
